  "definition": "A geostationary orbit is a circular, prograde orbit in Earth's equatorial plane with an orbital period equal to Earth's sidereal rotation. A spacecraft in this ideal orbit remains above one longitude and appears stationary to an observer fixed on Earth.[^1] These conditions make geostationary orbit a strict subset of geosynchronous orbit.",
